---
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  lang="en"
  path="/en/changelog/"
  title="mclip Changelog"
  description="Public release notes for mclip."
>
  <main class="text-page">
    <a class="back-link" href="/en/">Back home</a>
    <h1>Changelog</h1>
    <article class="release-note">
      <p class="eyebrow">In development</p>
      <h2>mclip-cli versioning and verified upgrades</h2>
      <p>
        Agent CLI preferences will distinguish missing, outdated, unknown legacy, current, and newer installations, with the matching install, upgrade, or reinstall action and no automatic downgrade.
      </p>
      <p>
        The desktop app will download the Release CLI matching its own version plus the SHA-256 companion, verify it, and recoverably replace the user-level binary. The public installer follows the same integrity contract.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="release-note">
      <p class="eyebrow">0.1.1</p>
      <h2>Polished core experience</h2>
      <p>
        Completes the Tailwind CSS 4 UI migration and adds System/Light/Dark appearance, configurable main and archive counts, row numbers, and main-window branding. Large histories scroll only the middle region, archive windows size to rendered content, and hover details use an independent window with consistent detail-owned deletion.
      </p>
      <p>
        Also improves color-code, emoji, long-file-name, and full-path presentation. mclip-cli help/version no longer reads history, and the public installer prefers prebuilt Release binaries.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="release-note">
      <p class="eyebrow">0.1.0</p>
      <h2>First public release</h2>
      <p>
        Adds tray clipboard history for macOS and Windows, text/image/file history with file restore, search, independent preview windows, preferences, and Chinese/English UI.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter lang="en" />
</SiteLayout>
